r forever chemicals","src":"Stock Titan","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxQQ0RpbHRLblRYNzBMaXZRa3hha25aeVNfLXY1Q2dTZUNLMzY2M2wtY3dyRjZYUzlSZWp6Tm1mOFFSVVFFeDNHc2paWXRDSVNMUS1fRnI2YWd4S1VqWE9sMlZPVW1PSDNiWGc1WWNyd3VRcnVwcFVpLWRnYjhaa2tjZzd0TTVhUWJsVUQwcXdxdldBZ2lGQ0ZlaVZPdmt1V2x5TVVuMjZ2dE5lbVNieUlkanI0dHNlNDNaZEh1UGxn?oc=5","date":"2026-10-27","zh":"塞勒姆水廠每天可處理多達 200 萬加侖的永久化學品"}],"order_news":[{"title":"American Water Works Company, I (AWK) Q3 FY2026 earnings call transcript","src":"Yahoo Finance","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiigFBVV95cUxNRnBGVFVmNTItbnB3NzN6RUJ4NXdtODBIT1NFTzZEUDdMaUVHd0xpMzNWd3F6MndUMlVGSTlBQ09sdmVKQUhwSGkxNU80a3ZkeTRQQUtzQ0lfUVdGZWRiaDJFS210WlNtNWJfNmh6VnB1QkxwLVY2Y1RWN24yUWNLbmJqeThWYmZaemc?oc=5","date":"2026-10-29","zh":"美國水務公司 (AWK) 2026 財年第三季財報電話會議紀錄"},{"title":"[American Water Works Q3 2026 Earnings Call] AWK Guides 2027 EPS to $6.53–$6.63, 8% Growth, as Essential Merger Nears Q1 2027 Close","src":"BigGo Finance","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE5faUNOaG1sb3BYWTFYRVRCZ2hESFNHZFVIcmx4a1BpMzA3TjRmRVlOdlpYaGo0dld1cm5mZ1hqS2xmWTg4cHRPS0lSclFCUDJjTmhfRzZFcWZGNkxm?oc=5","date":"2026-10-29","zh":"[美國水務公司 2026 年第三季財報電話會議] AWK 預計 2027 年每股收益為 6.53-6.63 美元，成長 8%，因為基本合併接近 2027 年第一季結束"},{"title":"AWK Q3 FY2026 earnings call","src":"finance.biggo.com","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTE9LOERzLXo3cEFVYzRDNi1EWkpEYUFLWEtXeVNTQ3l5bmlFdE9QdTU3Wl84MnpYQVNsRjdUMi1pcWU3VUdpbjVXUzdnNU1hdEJGZUtBcHhxQUQwUE9xNkhMcXRrWGIzRGVuZVNITTB2cnU3SzZfRmc?oc=5","date":"2026-10-29","zh":"AWK 2026 財年第三季財報電話會議"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":6},{"name":"併購","count":2}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-18","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1410636/000141063626000034/awk-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"With a history dating back to 1886, American Water is the largest and most geographically diverse, publicly-traded water and wastewater utility company in the United States, as measured by both operating revenues and population served. A holding company originally incorporated in Delaware in 1936, the Company employs approximately 7,000 professionals who provide drinking water, wastewater and other related services to approximately 14 million people in 24 states. The Company conducts the majority of its business through regulated utilities that provide water and wastewater services, collectively presented as one reportable segment, referred to as the \"Regulated Businesses.\" The Company also operates other businesses that provide water and wastewater services to the U.S. government on military installations, as well as municipalities. Individually, these other businesses do not meet the c","zh":"美國水務公司的歷史可以追溯到 1886 年，從營業收入和服務人口來看，它是美國最大、地域最多元化的公開交易的供水和污水處理公司。該公司最初於 1936 年在特拉華州註冊成立，是一家控股公司，擁有約 7,000 名專業人員，為 24 個州的約 1,400 萬人提供飲用水、廢水處理和其他相關服務。該公司透過提供水和廢水處理服務的受監管公用事業公司開展大部分業務，這些公用事業公司統稱為一個可報告部門，稱為「受監管業務」。該公司還經營其他業務，為美國政府的軍事設施以及市政當局提供供水和廢水處理服務。個別而言，這些其他業務不符合 c"},{"en":"On October 26, 2025, parent company entered into an Agreement and Plan of Merger (the \"Essential Merger Agreement\") with Essential to combine the two companies in a stock-for-stock transaction. The Essential Merger Agreement provides that, upon the completion of the proposed merger, Essential's shareholders will receive 0.305 shares of parent company common stock in exchange for each share of Essential common stock eligible for exchange in the merger. Upon completion of the proposed merger, Essential will be a wholly owned subsidiary of parent company, and parent company will retain its existing name and remain headquartered in Camden, New Jersey. The completion of the proposed merger is subject to certain customary conditions. The Company currently estimates that the closing of the proposed merger will occur by the end of the first quarter of 2027. See Note 5—Mergers, Acquisitions and D","zh":"2025 年 10 月 26 日，母公司與 Essential 簽訂了合併協議和計畫（「基本合併協議」），透過股票換股票交易合併兩家公司。 Essential 合併協議規定，在擬議合併完成後，Essential 股東將獲得 0.305 股母公司普通股，以換取每股符合合併條件的 Essential 普通股。在擬議合併完成後，Essential 將成為母公司的全資子公司，母公司將保留其現有名稱，總部仍位於新澤西州卡姆登。擬議合併的完成須滿足某些慣例條件。該公司目前預計擬議合併將於 2027 年第一季末完成。參見註 5——合併、收購和 D"},{"en":"Throughout this Annual Report on Form 10-K, unless the context otherwise requires, references to \"we,\" \"us,\" \"our,\" the \"Company,\" and \"American Water\" mean American Water Works Company, Inc. and its subsidiaries as of the date hereof, taken together as a whole. References to \"parent company\" mean American Water Works Company, Inc., without its subsidiaries.","zh":"在本表格 10-K 年度報告中，除非上下文另有要求，否則提及的「我們」、「我們的」、「本公司」和「Ame​​rican Water」均指 American Water Works Company, Inc. 及其截至本報告日期的子公司，作為一個整體。所提及的「母公司」是指 American Water Works Company, Inc.，不包括其子公司。"}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"The Company's Regulated Businesses have a large and geographically diverse customer base. A customer is defined as a person, business, municipality or any other entity that purchases the Company's water or wastewater services as of the last business day of a reporting period. One single customer may purchase the Company's services for use by multiple individuals or businesses. Examples of these customers are homes, apartment complexes, businesses and governmental entities.","zh":"該公司的受監管業務擁有龐大且分佈廣泛的客戶群。客戶被定義為截至報告期間最後一個工作日購買公司供水或污水處理服務的個人、企業、市政當局或任何其他實體。一名客戶可以購買公司的服務供多個個人或企業使用。這些客戶的例子包括家庭、公寓大樓、企業和政府實體。"},{"en":"The vast majority of the Company's regulated water customers are metered, which allows the Company to measure and bill for its customers' water usage, typically on a monthly basis. The Company employs a variety of methods of customer meter reading to monitor consumption. These methods range from meters with mechanical registers where consumption is manually recorded by meter readers, to meters with electronic registers capable of transmitting consumption data to proximity devices or via radio frequency to mobile or fixed network data collectors. The Company's wastewater customers are billed either a flat rate or based upon their water consumption.","zh":"本公司絕大多數受監管的用水客戶均採用計量表，這使得公司能夠測量客戶的用水量併計費（通常按月）。本公司採用多種顧客抄表方法來監控消費狀況。這些方法的範圍從具有機械寄存器的儀表（由抄表器手動記錄消耗量）到帶有電子寄存器的儀表，能夠將消耗數據傳輸到鄰近設備或通過射頻傳輸到移動或固定網路數據收集器。該公司的廢水處理客戶可以統一費率或根據其用水量付費。"}],"competition":[{"en":"The Company's Regulated Businesses generally do not face direct competition in their existing markets because (i) the Company operates in those markets pursuant to franchises, charters, certificates of public convenience and necessity or similar authorizations (collectively, \"CPCNs\") issued by state PUCs or other authorities, and (ii) the high cost of constructing a new water and wastewater system in an existing market creates a significant barrier to market entry. However, the Company's Regulated Businesses face competition from governmental agencies, other investor-owned utilities, large industrial customers with the ability to provide their own water supply/treatment process and strategic buyers that are entering new markets and/or making strategic acquisitions. When pursuing acquisitions, the Company's largest investor-owned competitors, based on a comparison of operating revenues an","zh":"本公司的受監管業務在現有市場中通常不會面臨直接競爭，因為 (i) 公司根據州公用事業委員會或其他當局頒發的特許經營權、特許權、公共便利和必要性證書或類似授權（統稱為“CPCN”）在這些市場中運營，以及 (ii) 在現有市場中建設新的供水和廢水處理系統的高成本對市場進入造成了重大障礙。然而，該公司的受監管業務面臨著來自政府機構、其他投資者擁有的公用事業公司、有能力提供自己的供水/處理流程的大型工業客戶以及正在進入新市場和/或進行策略性收購的策略買家的競爭。在進行收購時，根據營業收入和競爭對手的比較，公司最大的投資者擁有的競爭對手"},{"en":"All or portions of the Regulated Businesses' utility assets could be acquired by state, municipal or other government entities through one or more of the following methods: (i) eminent domain (also known as condemnation); (ii) the right of purchase given or reserved by a municipality or political subdivision when the original CPCN was granted; and (iii) the right of purchase given or reserved under the law of the state in which the utility subsidiary was incorporated or from which it received its CPCN. The acquisition consideration related to such a proceeding initiated by a local government may be determined consistent with applicable eminent domain law, or may be negotiated or fixed by appraisers as prescribed by the law of the state or the jurisdiction of the particular CPCN.","zh":"州、市或其他政府實體可以透過以下一種或多種方法收購受監管企業的全部或部分公用事業資產： (i) 徵用權（也稱為徵用）； (ii) 在授予原始 CPCN 時由市政府或政治分區給予或保留的購買權； (iii) 根據公用事業子公司成立國或從公用事業獲得 CPCN 的國家的法律賦予或保留的購買權。與地方政府發起的此類程序相關的收購對價可以根據適用的徵用權法確定，也可以根據州法律或特定 CPCN 管轄區的規定由評估師協商或確定。"}],"segments":{},"peers":["AWR","XYL","CWT","AEP","WEC"]}}